    "http://jobs.shu.edu/cw/en-us/job/497368/assistant-professor-of-law-and-director-of-legal-externships-and-public-interest": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities - Seton Hall University, New Jersey Javascript must be enabled for the correct page display Skip to Content Close Close Academics Back Academics Academic Programs Back Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Continuing Education Online Programs Dual Degree Programs Certificate Programs Special Programs Summer Sessions Schools and Colleges Back Schools and Colleges Arts and Sciences Business Communication and the Arts Diplomacy and International Relations Education and Human Services Health and Medical Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Theology Additional Resources Back Additional Resources Our Faculty Departments Centers and Institutes University Core Curriculum University Libraries Academic Calendar Assessment Office of the Provost Admissions Back Admissions Undergraduate Graduate Catholic Mission Back Catholic Mission Catholic Mission Back Catholic Mission Mission and Ministry Priest Community Catholic Studies Theology Additional Resources Back Additional Resources Mass Schedule Centers and Institutes Archdiocese Athletics Back Athletics Athletics Resources Back Athletics Resources SHUPirates.com Schedules Tickets Pirate Blue Get Connected SHUPirates.com Alumni Back Alumni Alumni and Friends Back Athletics Resources Alumni Home Alumni Directory Share Your News Benefits and Services E-mail Accounts Request a Transcript True Blue Support Seton Hall Back Support Seton Hall Why Seton Hall? Ways to Give About Back About Why Seton Hall? Ways to Give Events PirateNet Support SHU Menu About Events PirateNet SUPPORT SHU Academics Admissions Catholic Mission Athletics Alumni Search by keyword or location e.g. \"Administrator, Professor, Technology, etc.\" Full time / Part time Full-time 1 Locations Newark 1 Categories Faculty 1 Already Applied? Update your details and view your application progress. Login Subscribe Keep informed about job opportunities at Seton Hall University Job Alert Human Resources Seton Hall Mission Statement Seton Hall: A Catholic University Human Resources Home Careers at Seton Hall Thank you for your interest in working with Seton Hall University. All applicants must create an online application to be considered for any open position. Please note, employment is contingent upon satisfactory criminal and other relevant background investigations. The determination of satisfactory is at the sole discretion of Seton Hall University. Resumes received outside of the online application process will not be accepted. If special accommodations are needed in order to apply for a position, please contact the Department of Human Resources . Assistant Professor of Law and Director of Legal Externships and Public Interest Apply now Job no: 497368 Full time/Part time: Full-time Location: Newark Categories: Faculty Seton Hall Law School seeks to hire an Assistant Professor of Law and Director of Legal Externships and Public Interest. This is a non-tenure track position. The Director works collaboratively with the Office of Career Services and the Associate Dean for Experiential Education, while maintaining primary responsibility for the academic integrity, assessment, and accreditation of the Externship Program. Core responsibilities include providing academic leadership of the externship curriculum, ensuring compliance with ABA standards, student advising and mentoring, placement development and employer outreach, and developing of public interest programming. Duties and Responsibilities: Externship Program • Direct and administer the externship program to provide students with experiential learning opportunities that foster professional identity formation, ethical judgment, and the development of professional competencies. • Manage enrollment processes, eligibility determinations, registration procedures, and program communications for all externship offerings. Update materials and relevant websites as needed. • Update Memorandum of Understanding with externship placements and other contracts as needed. • Serve as the Law School’s primary administrator responsible for ensuring compliance with ABA Standard 304 and other applicable accreditation requirements governing field placement programs. • Develop and maintain relationships with judges, government agencies, public interest organizations, prosecutors' offices, public defenders, corporate legal departments, and law firms to expand and diversify externship opportunities for students. Recruit, evaluate, and approve new placements. • Monitor placement performance and implement corrective action to meet educational standards. • Develop instructional materials and teach the classroom component of the externship program, including seminars that integrate doctrine, professional identity formation, ethics, reflective practice, and professional skills development. • Communicate regularly with students regarding placement experiences. • Review supervisor evaluations of students and evaluate all assigned student work. • Maintain records to ensure compliance with ABA standards. • Develop, assess, and periodically revise student learning outcomes for the Externship Program; collect and analyze assessment data; and implement program improvements based on assessment results. • Prepare reports and recommendations regarding program effectiveness and student outcomes. Public Interest Programming • Develop and implement strategic initiatives that advance the Law School's public interest mission and increase student engagement in public service careers in collaboration with Career Services and faculty. • Coordinate public interest programming, networking events, speaker programs, and related initiatives and develop relationships with public interest organizations and governmental agencies to expand student opportunities. • Advise students regarding public interest career opportunities, fellowships, and postgraduate opportunities. • Assist in administration of public interest funding, fellowships, loan repayment programs, stipends, or pro bono initiatives, as assigned. • Support fundraising for public interest initiatives and events. Faculty Teaching and Service • Participate in faculty meetings, committees, and other governance activities consistent with faculty status and university policies. • Engage in professional development and maintain familiarity with developments in experiential legal education and ABA accreditation requirements. • Represent Seton Hall Law at relevant events as appropriate. • Teach elective courses related to professional development and experiential learning as required and appropriate to meet faculty course load. Required Qualifications: • J.D. degree from an ABA-accredited law school. • Admission to practice law in at least one U.S. jurisdiction. • Minimum of five years of legal practice or closely related professional experience, including experience in judicial, governmental, public interest, nonprofit, corporate, or private practice settings. • Demonstrated commitment to experiential legal education and student mentoring. • Excellent organizational, interpersonal, and written communication skills. Desired Qualifications: • Prior teaching experience in legal education. • Experience teaching or supervising students in experiential learning environments. • Experience supervising law students, attorneys, or legal professionals. • Experience administering externship, clinical, public interest, or experiential learning programs. • Familiarity with ABA accreditation standards governing field placements and experiential education. • Demonstrated experience developing professional relationships with legal employers, judges, government agencies, nonprofit organizations, or other legal placement partners. Salary Range: $92,965 - $103,295 Exempt/Nonexempt: Exempt Physical Demands: General Office Environment Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit three professional references. Benefits Information: Full Time Benefits Life today is complex. That’s why Seton Hall University offers a comprehensive package of benefits and programs to help you simplify and enrich your life. These benefits are important elements of your total university compensation package. Benefits include but are not limited to bundled medical, prescription, and vision insurance, dental insurance, and life insurance, and retirement plan. More information is available at https://www.shu.edu/human-resources/benefits.html . Seton Hall University is located in South Orange, New Jersey, 14 miles from New York City. It is the oldest Catholic diocesan institution of higher education in the United States and is home to about 6,300 undergraduate and 3,700 graduate students. A vibrant and culturally inclusive community, Seton Hall pursues academic excellence and ethical development in a collaborative environment and prepares its students to be servant leaders in their professional and community lives. Seton Hall University is an equal opportunity employer. It honors diverse perspectives and welcomes employees from all faith traditions. In turn, its employees respect Catholic beliefs and values, engage in servant leadership, and support the University’s mission as a Catholic institution of higher education. Advertised: 20 Jul 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Assistant Professor of Law and Director of Legal Externships and Public Interest Newark Expression of interest Loading... Current opportunities Position Location Closes Assistant Professor of Law and Director of Legal Externships and Public Interest Newark Powered by PageUp Seton Hall University 400 South Orange Ave South Orange , NJ 07079 (973) 761-9000 Privacy Statements Title IX Nondiscrimination Statement and Information Contact Us Student Services Parents and Families Career Center Technology Web Accessibility Site Map Visiting Campus Public Safety Disability Support Services Campus Security Report Employment Follow #SetonHall Back to top"
